# Sentinel: rules for AI coding assistants

Read CLAUDE.md first; it is the source of truth. Summary of the rules that matter most:

Project
- Monorepo: packages/engine (pure domain logic), apps/api (Cloudflare Worker, Hono, D1), apps/web (React + Vite).
- Verify every change with: npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build.

Never
- Never let a requester decide their own request, in any code path.
- Never allow a flow definition where a path finishes without a human approval.
- Never give the AI drafter a way to activate a flow or decide a task; it edits drafts only.
- Never update or delete rows in audit_events, or change an active flow version.
- Never store a superior or approver per person; compute it from org_units and the authority matrix.
- Never swallow a rule evaluation error to fall through to another rule; fail closed.
- Never commit secrets, tokens, or account credentials.
- Never import the engine package root from apps/web; use @sentinel/engine/model.

Always
- Put domain rules in packages/engine with a test; keep I/O in apps/api.
- Persist state changes together with their audit events in one database batch.
- Add an MCP tool in apps/api/src/mcp.ts for every new API endpoint.
- Write user-visible text in plain English, sentence case; leave data values and identifiers untranslated.
- Use TypeScript strict mode; avoid `any`.
- Follow apps/web/DESIGN.md for UI: color only for status and actions, tokens from :root, no new one-off colors.
